      "constraints": "The quote identifies the target for this taster only; it does not quantify this population or their specific motivations beyond being 'unsure'."
    },
    {
      "field": "rationale",
      "claim": "Focusing the piece on lowering arrival/startup friction is justified because informal feedback emphasised the 'welcome' as the main return reason and the choir chose to retain a later entry window.",
      "sourceEvidence": "After the October rehearsal, twelve of the nineteen people present answered a short question about returning. Eight mentioned the welcome, three mentioned the songs, and one mentioned both. Two people who had missed the previous rehearsal said late trains had played a part. The choir agreed at its monthly meeting to keep the later entry window through December.",
      "inference": "The micro‑survey counts show 'welcome' was the most-cited reason for returning; the committee's recorded operational choice to keep a later entry window is an action consistent with reducing arrival friction — together these facts support an editorial angle emphasising welcome and arrival practicalities.",
      "constraints": "The source gives counts from a short, informal question and a recorded decision without explaining committee motives; it does not establish causal effects (e.g., that later entry increases attendance) nor report a representative survey."
