      "sourceEvidence": "After the October rehearsal, twelve of the nineteen people present answered a short question about returning. Eight mentioned the welcome, three mentioned the songs, and one mentioned both. Two people who had missed the previous rehearsal said late trains had played a part. The choir agreed at its monthly meeting to keep the later entry window through December. The minutes record the decision without an account of why it was chosen. There has been no survey of confidence before and after singing and no comparison with a fixed-start rehearsal.",
      "inference": "This contiguous block contains the rehearsal feedback (counts and reasons), the committee decision and its unreported rationale, and the explicit data gap; these constitute the primary evidence items that anchor the editorial opportunity and its limits.",
      "constraints": "The evidence is limited to what the source reports: an informal short question answered by a subset of attendees, recorded minutes lacking rationale, and an absence of formal surveys — it does not provide broader longitudinal data or tested interventions."
    }
  ]
